WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.204 --> 00:00:21.870
Riley Clark lowered the car window and gazed at the brand-new bike track.

2
00:00:21.871 --> 00:00:26.304
It twisted through a huge green field like a brown snake.

3
00:00:26.305 --> 00:00:33.881
Dirt had been piled up here and there to form jumps. A big mud pit looked like trouble for riders.

4
00:00:33.882 --> 00:00:43.048
Riley's heartbeat sped up when she spotted the Blue Demons team banner—and the large crowd.

5
00:00:43.049 --> 00:00:46.299
"Nervous, Riley?" her father asked.

6
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:51.716
"Who, me?" Riley joked. "Nerves-of-Steel Riley?"

7
00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:58.937
Then she paused. "A little," she admitted. "I really want to make the team."

8
00:00:58.938 --> 00:01:02.891
The Blue Demons were the best mountain bike team in the state.

9
00:01:02.892 --> 00:01:09.027
Today's event was an open practice, which meant anyone could ride and test the track.

10
00:01:09.028 --> 00:01:14.011
The Blue Demons were holding the real team tryout next Saturday.

11
00:01:14.012 --> 00:01:21.895
"You'll do great!" Riley's older sister, Jordan, grabbed the headrest and pulled herself forward from the backseat.

12
00:01:21.896 --> 00:01:25.665
"Don't let all these people rattle you."

13
00:01:25.666 --> 00:01:32.322
"I'm not scared," Riley replied. "I eat fear for breakfast!"

14
00:01:32.323 --> 00:01:39.409
Jordan laughed. "That's my line. But I'll let you borrow it today.

15
00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:44.248
And don't forget—where your brain goes, your body will follow."

16
00:01:44.249 --> 00:01:52.733
Jordan was 17, five years older than Riley. Riley had started mountain biking because Jordan was a rider.

17
00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:57.643
But Riley had quickly discovered her own fierce love of the sport.

18
00:01:57.644 --> 00:02:05.460
Unfortunately, Jordan hadn't been on a bike for months—not since a terrible bike accident last fall.

19
00:02:05.461 --> 00:02:13.048
She was still recovering from the crash; she wore a brace on one leg and used crutches to walk.

20
00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:25.260
Mr. Clark walked around to the rack on the back of the car and helped Riley remove her battered but beloved Supertrek.

21
00:02:25.261 --> 00:02:29.455
It had been Jordan's first bike, her lucky bike.

22
00:02:29.456 --> 00:02:39.178
Riley parked her bike, and then she and her father got into line at a tent to register.

23
00:02:39.179 --> 00:02:42.734
"Want us to stay with you?" Mr. Clark asked.

24
00:02:42.735 --> 00:02:46.106
"I'll be fine, Dad. It's only practice."

25
00:02:46.107 --> 00:02:54.020
"Okay. We'll all be here for the tryout next weekend, rooting for you."

26
00:02:54.021 --> 00:03:04.332
Mr. Clark signed some registration forms, and Riley pulled out her new prized possession: an official USA Cycling license.

27
00:03:04.333 --> 00:03:13.036
Coach Adams, the Blue Demons head coach, spotted it. "Congratulations on becoming a member of USA Cycling, Riley!"

28
00:03:13.037 --> 00:03:15.669
"Thanks, Coach."

29
00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:19.928
"You'll need that license next week at the tryout," he added.

30
00:03:19.929 --> 00:03:25.393
"Today the junior division riders will ride the practice trail from ten to eleven o'clock."

31
00:03:25.394 --> 00:03:27.941
"Cool," Riley said.

32
00:03:27.942 --> 00:03:34.237
A few minutes later, she walked her father back to the car.

33
00:03:34.238 --> 00:03:38.027
"We'll be back at eleven," he said, looking worried.

34
00:03:38.028 --> 00:03:40.807
"I'll be careful, I promise."

35
00:03:40.808 --> 00:03:49.459
He gave her a quick kiss on the forehead. "Love you, peanut. Now go and eat them for breakfast!"

36
00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:59.287
"It's fear, Dad," Riley said patiently. "I eat fear for breakfast, not other riders. I'm not a zombie."

37
00:03:59.288 --> 00:04:03.871
"But you sure look like one!" Jordan yelled from the car.

38
00:04:03.872 --> 00:04:11.285
"Brains!" Riley clawed at the car window. "I need brains!"

39
00:04:11.286 --> 00:04:22.518
"Nice zombie impression," Jordan said. "Just don't ride like one!"

40
00:04:22.519 --> 00:04:31.836
After Jordan and Dad left, Riley checked her phone. It was nine thirty. She had thirty minutes to study the track.

41
00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:36.343
Mountain bike races were not races against individual riders.

42
00:04:36.344 --> 00:04:45.685
Each rider raced against the clock, and the rider with the fastest time won. So knowing the track in advance definitely paid off.

43
00:04:45.686 --> 00:04:53.749
Riley walked along the dirt trail, memorizing the location of soft spots and mud pits.

44
00:04:53.750 --> 00:05:00.574
She tried to gauge which turns and jumps she could take at full speed, and which ones would require more control.

45
00:05:00.575 --> 00:05:07.732
She also had to calculate how fast she could take the straightaways before going airborne for a jump.

46
00:05:07.733 --> 00:05:15.073
Looking at the jumps suddenly made Riley feel nervous again. Jordan had crashed while making a jump.

47
00:05:15.074 --> 00:05:19.207
She'd been in the lead at the Racing Raptors track on Hawk Mountain.

48
00:05:19.208 --> 00:05:24.232
Then Jordan went airborne for the jump and flew off her bike.

49
00:05:24.233 --> 00:05:29.644
She'd landed hard, and there was blood and an ambulance and—

50
00:05:29.645 --> 00:05:35.817
"Hey, watch where you're going!" A girl glared at Riley. "You almost knocked me over."

51
00:05:35.818 --> 00:05:40.028
"Sorry!" Riley said. "I didn't see you there."

52
00:05:40.029 --> 00:05:46.289
"Really? I'm not invisible," the girl snapped. She looked about the same age as Riley.

53
00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:51.542
She was tall, with leg muscles that showed she was an experienced rider.

54
00:05:51.543 --> 00:05:58.541
"Sorry," Riley apologized again. Then the girl's glittering bike caught her eye.

55
00:05:58.542 --> 00:06:06.279
"Wow! Is that the latest Fleet HD3? I didn't know it came with 24-inch wheels."

56
00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:15.518
"It doesn't." The girl strapped on her helmet. "My dad had this bike custom-built for me.

57
00:06:15.519 --> 00:06:22.431
For a huge amount of money, of course. I plan to make the team, and I need the best bike money can buy."

58
00:06:22.432 --> 00:06:27.419
Several replies raced through Riley's mind, none of them very nice.

59
00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:33.225
Luckily she heard her dad's voice inside her head: "Eat them for breakfast!"

60
00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:37.018
That made Riley smile instead of saying something nasty.

61
00:06:37.019 --> 00:06:46.410
Meanwhile the girl was staring at Riley's Supertrek, with its chipped paint and worn seat. "Your bike looks pretty old."

62
00:06:46.411 --> 00:06:56.405
"Yeah. It's a hand-me-down from my sister. My parents said I can get a new bike soon. But for now it's okay," Riley added.

63
00:06:56.406 --> 00:07:04.216
"I won a bunch of races on it last year. And I'm counting on it to get me the best time at the tryout next week too!"

64
00:07:04.217 --> 00:07:08.289
The girl's eyes narrowed. "We'll see about that!"

65
00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:15.542
She jumped on her bike and rode to the starting line.

66
00:07:15.543 --> 00:07:24.289
Riley followed as Delaney Thompson, the Blue Demons team captain, began making an announcement.

67
00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:29.947
As usual, his long dreadlocks hung in a cascade down his back.

68
00:07:29.948 --> 00:07:38.703
"Okay, everyone," he began. "This practice trail is a mile long, and we'll use it for the tryout trail next week too.

69
00:07:38.704 --> 00:07:44.027
Each of you can take as many practice runs today as you want during your division's hour.

70
00:07:44.028 --> 00:07:49.532
Riders will push off every thirty seconds, so pay attention and stay in line.

71
00:07:49.533 --> 00:07:54.183
When you're finished with one run, go to the back of the line to wait for another."

72
00:07:54.184 --> 00:08:04.276
All the junior riders jostled to get a place in line, and Riley noticed the girl with the expensive bike had managed to be first.

73
00:08:04.277 --> 00:08:12.491
Delaney blew his whistle and pressed his stopwatch, and the girl flew down the track.

74
00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:26.674
Riley watched as she hit each jump and took the curves like a pro. "Whoa. Who is that girl?"

75
00:08:26.675 --> 00:08:35.231
Delaney scanned the list on his clipboard. "New kid named Quinn Evans. She just moved here from Colorado."

76
00:08:35.232 --> 00:08:41.571
He looked up. "Fast turns aren't everything, Riley," he added softly.

77
00:08:41.572 --> 00:08:54.690
"Oh, and I have some bad news for girls trying out for the junior division. There are just two open spots on the team."
